### Q3. Rigorous-Randomised Side

- **Re-examining `nested Prop R2`:** `Prop R2` ([nested_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L332-L358) §4) only floors designs *without algebraic children* at $2/5$ `[heuristic]`. Earlier work assumed algebraic children required joint control of $> d+1$ evaluation points (`Lemma OD`, [nested_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L362-L398) §5). Phases 25–31 bypassed `Lemma OD` at depth 2 **without GRH** via union-bound + parent-count decoupling (`Prop UB`, `Prop DC`, [pc3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L128-L166) §2), reaching $L_N[\alpha]$ for every $\alpha \in (3/8, 2/5)$ and $L_N[3/8]$ (under $a > 2c_2$) from published external inputs (`Theorem 2L-MF`, [mf2L_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L46-L60) §0; conditional on the unrefereed internal chain plus `audit2L`'s open write-up of `Hyp U′` under design `DW`, [audit2L_audit.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md#L76-L78) §0) `[proved]`.
- **What GRH discharges vs. leaves untouched:**
  - *At $2/5$ and $[3/8, 2/5)$:* `Theorem U-MF` ([mfU_theorem.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mfU_theorem.md#L60-L65) §0) and `Theorem 2L-MF` ([mf2L_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L46-L60) §0) are already GRH-free. Dirichlet GRH trivially supplies small-conductor character twists `Hyp SC` (already proved unconditionally via Drappeau CJM 2015 Props 2.9/2.13, [mf2L_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L52-L55) §0), while Dedekind GRH supplies growing-degree quadratic characters (`Lemma X_ERH`, [nested_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L426-L446) §7), simplifying `U-MF` square certification ([mfU_theorem.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mfU_theorem.md#L624-L660) §8.4). Neither lowers any exponent, discharges the internal chain (`LD*`, `L2_fam`, `RAT`, `SPR-P′`, `AB₂`, `U′`-under-`DW`), or removes the combinatorial squarefree-part condition $a > 2c_2$ at $3/8$ ([thmAB_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L174) §1.3; [audit2L_audit.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md#L67-L68) §0) `[proved]`.
  - *Below $3/8$ ($4/11$ and depth $j \ge 4$):* **No version of GRH pushes below $3/8$** `[proved]`. Depth-$i$ decoupling requires relative pair variance $\phi_i \le \eta_i \asymp D^{-i\alpha}$ ([pc3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L348-L355) §7.5), whereas the *principal-character* (archimedean $\beta$-drift + gcd local-factor $\tau(\delta)$) variance is $\Omega(\gamma^2\lambda^2) = \Omega(D^{-2\alpha})$ even if all non-principal character errors vanish (`Lemmas LF-A, OPV-A`, [thmAB_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L379-L413) §6). Thus $4/11$ ($i=2$) stays borderline and depth $j \ge 4$ ($i \ge 3$) fails regardless of GRH `[heuristic]`.
  - *Rigorous $L[1/3]$ NFS:* **Still conditional** `[proved]`. GRH discharges neither all-target algebraic supply `Hyp AD` in `Theorem NR` ([nested_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L485-L500) §8) nor 2-adic Bockstein fruitfulness (`Conjecture F` / Lee–Venkatesan `Conj 7.1`, [fruit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/fruit_results.md#L64-L75) §0; [detGRH_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L299-L308) §3). *One new angle under Dirichlet GRH:* applying `zroute`'s deterministic unit-elimination `Lemma XK-Z` + Miller splitting `Prop PIN` ([zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L135-L155) §2, [zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L211-L220) §2, [zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L312-L316) §3.2) to Lee–Venkatesan's unconditional randomized $L[1/3]$ relations ([README.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/README.md#L16-L18)) replaces 2-adic `Conj 7.1` by **rational $\mathbb{Q}$-pinning (`PIN` on primes $q \le 2\ln^2 N$)** summed across $J = L_N[1/3]$ independent LV fields `[proved]` — still unproved without hidden labels, but avoids 2-adic sign obstructions `[speculative]`.

---

### Q4. Below $L[1/3]$: Theorem vs. Sketched Method

- **GRH-as-theorem touches none of the five open doors positively** `[proved]`:
  - *`grdeg` relative-rank $\ge 3$ type-D ([grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L66-L80) §0) & $G_r \to L[1/4]$ model ([midk_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/midk_results.md#L39-L65) §0):* Pure Diophantine height / infinite-unit-volume ($V_F = \infty$) geometry; zero-free strips neither build degenerate modules nor bound $\mathcal{O}_k^\times$-orbits.
  - *`Prop SI` ($L[1/3, 1.2114]$, [suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L318-L343) §1.4; [sicheck_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/sicheck_results.md#L538-L596) §5):* Constant-only ($\alpha = 1/3$); RH short-interval smoothness stops at $h \ge X^{1/2+\varepsilon}$ ([genus2rh_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/genus2rh_results.md#L546-L570) §7.2), far above $L_X[2/3] = X^{o(1)}$, and gives existence rather than an $L^{o(1)}$ constructor ([siconstruct_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L92-L155) §2.1).
  - *Single $a_f(N)$ ([cuspcoef_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cuspcoef_results.md#L196) §2.2, [cuspcoef_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cuspcoef_results.md#L379-L392) §5):* GRH only *tightens* the `Theorem DFB` barrier ($B = O(\log\log p)$); native algorithms stay $\ge N^{1/2+o(1)}$.
  - *`PRIM` ([prim_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/prim_results.md#L338-L346) §3; [completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L225-L235) §5.4):* GRH only bounds fixed-base exceptional primes (a barrier, defeated at large height); $O(1)$-bit leaks remain exponential ([completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L171-L174) §4).
- **Can `remark.pdf`'s *method* ($\sqrt{X}$ theta lifts, Guinand–Weil variance, path quadric, Bost slope) yield tools that do?**
  - *Smooth numbers near $kN$ (`Prop SI`):* **No** `[heuristic]`. Bandwidth $X/h \approx X^{1-o(1)}$ is swamped by *on-line* ($\operatorname{Re}\rho = 1/2$) diagonal zero variance ($\sqrt{X}$ lifts amplify off-line zeros, not on-line noise), and explicit-formula positivity is non-constructive ([conn_ana.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/conn_ana.md#L38-L41) §0 P2; [siconstruct_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L299) §3).
  - *Smooth BDH / pair correlation in progressions:* **No sub-$1/3$ gain** `[proved]`. Finite-depth descent ladders satisfy $\alpha_j = (j+1)/(3j+2) > 1/3$ ([midk_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/midk_results.md#L39-L49) §0), and depth $\ge 4$ dies on principal-character variance $D^{-2\alpha}$, not progression error.
  - *Character/point-count bounds beating Burgess:* **No sub-$1/3$ gain** `[proved]`. GRH *already* beats Burgess down to polylog length, and `dsr` (`Thm FN`/`SB`) + `cov38b` (`Lemma M`/`Thm B`, [cov38b_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cov38b_results.md#L399-L407) §2.4) prove character-sum bounds neither solve `DSR` nor beat $N^{1/5}$ via phase discarding. (Seesaw sums on the path quadric $x_1x_2+\dots+x_{k-1}x_k$ faintly echo `cov38b`'s phase-retaining $\ge 26$th-moment target at $q^{0.32}$, which only affects exponential $< N^{1/5}$ `[speculative]`.)
  - **Single most promising conversion touching sub-$L[1/3]$ (`grdeg` door (i), *barrier direction*):** **Bost's Arakelov slope inequality** (`[KNOWN]` published theorem, independent of `remark.pdf`'s validity) applied to evaluation maps on rank-$m \ge 3$ hermitian $\mathcal{O}_k$-bundles to bypass infinite unit volume ($V_F = \infty$) `[speculative]`. *Exact statement needed:* For any rank-$m \ge 3$ $\mathcal{O}_k$-submodule of $\mathcal{O}_K \times \mathcal{O}_{K'}$ ($[k:\mathbb{Q}] = e$ fixed, $r = me$, $[K:k] = n$) whose $m-1$ mod-$N$ linking conditions are not confined to a lower-rank sublattice, the Arakelov/Mahler generator heights satisfy $\max_{1 \le j \le m} h_k(w_j) \ge c(r/D)\log N - O(dn)$ for an absolute $c > 0$ — raising `grdeg` door (i) from model $L[1/4]$ back to $\alpha \ge 1/3$ ([grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L66-L80) §0).

---

### Q5. Verdict & Top Three Next Threads

- **Verdict:** **No credible path below $L[1/3]$** ($P < 1\text{–}2\%$) `[heuristic]`. Neither GRH/ERH nor `remark.pdf`'s analytic/theta-lift machinery lowers candidate norm sizes below the resultant / size–entropy floor ([suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L94-L96) Thm SS; [completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L62-L69) §0).
- **Ranked next threads:**
  1. **Finish unconditional rigorous $L_N[3/8]$ (`U′` under `DW` + merged `2L-MF` note):**
     - *Target statement:* Write out `Hyp U′` under design `DW` ([audit2L_audit.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md#L76-L78) §0) and merge `2L-final` + `Lemma SPR-P′` + `mf2L` into one self-contained note ([README.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/README.md#L103-L106); [STATUS.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/STATUS.md#L373-L374)).
     - *Remark relevance:* **None** — already unconditional from published inputs `[proved]`.
     - *Probability / Cost:* **~80%**; **Low** (1–2 rounds).
  2. **Close `grdeg` door (i) via Bost's Arakelov slope inequality over $\mathcal{O}_k$:**
     - *Target statement:* Prove $\max_j h_k(w_j) \ge c(r/D)\log N - O(dn)$ for non-sublattice-confined relative-rank-$m \ge 3$ type-D modules, testing first on the $k=\mathbb{Q}(i), r=6$ witness ([STATUS.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/STATUS.md#L377); [grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L66-L80) §0).
     - *Remark relevance:* **Method-inspired only** — uses published Bost/Chambert-Loir slope inequalities, valid regardless of `remark.pdf` `[speculative]`.
     - *Probability / Cost:* **~30%** to close the barrier ($<2\%$ for a sub-$1/3$ algorithm); **Low–Medium** (1 round).
  3. **Conditional rigorous Las Vegas $L_N[1/3]$ via pooled LV fields + `XK-Z` + `Prop PIN`:**
     - *Target statement:* Under explicit Dirichlet GRH, test and try to prove `Prop PIN` ($e_q \in \sum_{j=1}^J W_j$ for all primes $q \le 2\ln^2 N$) across $J = L_N[1/3, c']$ independent Lee–Venkatesan fields ([zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L211-L220) §2, [zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L312-L316) §3.2) `[speculative]`.
     - *Remark relevance:* **High if Dirichlet GRH holds** — upgrades conditional `Dirichlet GRH ⇒ rigorous L[1/3]` to unconditional, and remains a publishable conditional theorem even if `remark.pdf` fails `[KNOWN]`.
     - *Probability / Cost:* **~10–15%**; **Medium** (1 toy-pooling + 1 proof round).

